From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: qcom: tsens: skip SM8550 uplow wake IRQ

Adaptation 7.2 de Pocknix/ROCKNIX 0203 : sur SM8550 l'IRQ uplow ordinaire
réveille s2idle immédiatement (pm_wakeup_irq pointe dessus à chaque
tentative) — on ne l'arme pas en wakeup sur qcom,sm8550 ; critical reste
armé. Notre 0204 masque déjà les seuils bas pendant le suspend.

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
index 51f20ef..6df6420 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
@@ -1320,10 +1320,16 @@ int tsens_suspend_common(struct tsens_priv *priv)
 	if (!device_may_wakeup(priv->dev))
 		return 0;
 
-	if (priv->feat->combo_int)
+	if (priv->feat->combo_int) {
 		enable_irq_wake(priv->combined_irq);
-	else {
-		enable_irq_wake(priv->uplow_irq);
+	} else {
+		/*
+		 * On SM8550 the ordinary uplow IRQ wakes s2idle immediately
+		 * (pm_wakeup_irq points at it on every attempt); leave it as
+		 * non-wakeup. Critical stays armed. (Pocknix/ROCKNIX 0203.)
+		 */
+		if (!of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,sm8550"))
+			enable_irq_wake(priv->uplow_irq);
 		if (priv->feat->crit_int)
 			enable_irq_wake(priv->crit_irq);
 	}
